# pq-verify (MIT) for the live i-nist test in CI only (tests/test_pqverify.py Live). PQ-Proof does not depend on it at run time.
# Library audits (--audit-kem, --audit-dsa) use none of its extras, so CI installs the wheel alone with --no-deps.
# pq-verify.txt pins the version the tests were written against (pqlite/impl.py PQV_TESTED) by the hash of its one
# platform-independent wheel, taken from the PyPI JSON API (2.19.0 was uploaded 2026-11-15, so no two-week cutoff was used).
# For a new version, change the line below and PQV_TESTED together, run the tests, and write the new wheel's
# digests.sha256 from https://pypi.org/pypi/pq-verify/<version>/json into pq-verify.txt (the wheel only, not the sdist).
pq-verify==2.19.0
